{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112100,"nonce":"R2NKbtKMa4OGW4CnfugMn9vSH5c=","title":"1.1 AutoRimmer skeleton: file protocol, verb registry, main-thread loop","message":"Wave 1 — substrate. Depends: 0.1 (findings may amend). Gates: every other wave-1+ spec.\n\n## Goal\nThe load-bearing skeleton: AutoRimmer mod with file protocol, verb registry,\nand main-thread execution loop. Every later spec plugs verbs into this.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §Architecture §Protocol §Conventions\n- `analyzerbridge/Source/AnalyzerBridge/CommandPoller.cs` (file half),\n  `BridgeGameComponent.cs` (main-thread half), `MiniJson.cs`, and\n  analyzerbridge/CLAUDE.md — this is the template; generalize, don't rewrite\n- `logrelay/Source/RelaySink.cs` — flusher pattern\n- `_mp/DETERMINISM.md` — the lazy-getter hazard (observers must not trigger\n  generation side effects)\n\n## Scope\n- Mod skeleton: About/ (packageId Dorian.AutoRimmer, load-order tail),\n  Source/AutoRimmer/*.csproj (net48, Release; reference Assembly-CSharp from\n  `_RimWorld-Agent`'s Managed/), Assemblies/ committed per workspace rules.\n- Protocol dirs under save-data `AutoRimmer/`: commands/, commands/done/,\n  results/, status.json (~1Hz heartbeat: game loaded, paused, speed, tick,\n  active op), journal/ (reserved for 1.2).\n- Envelope + error taxonomy per DESIGN.md §Protocol. Stale-command handling\n  copied from analyzerbridge (consume-before-execute, stale-on-restart).\n- Verb registry: registration mechanism (worker's choice: attribute scan or\n  explicit table), args accessor with typed getters + bad-args errors, each\n  verb declares main-thread requirement (default) and executes at the\n  GameComponentUpdate safe point. Long results streamed to file off-thread.\n- Built-in verbs: `ping`, `status`, `version` (game+mod versions, bench id).\n\n## Invariants\nObservers never mutate; file half never touches Verse; every consumed command\ngets exactly one result file, even on exception (code=exception + stack).\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nRegistry mechanism; arg validation depth; whether results carry a small state\nheader (tick, paused) on every response.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Builds Release; loads on `_RimWorld-Agent` with zero red errors.\n- ping/status/version round-trip via files; malformed JSON and unknown op\n  yield structured errors; kill -9 with a pending command → stale-on-restart\n  answered at next launch, not replayed.","files":null}]}